# Copy to /etc/astock-v2-rewrite.env and edit. The kernel never reads the wall
# clock; schedulers pass the trading day explicitly.
# Use a NEW path after the rewrite; legacy databases are refused on purpose.
# Every path below is absolute and inside the state directory the unit may
# write (StateDirectory=astock-v2-rewrite / ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/...):
# ProtectSystem=strict makes the rest of the filesystem read-only, so a
# relative default or a path under /var/lib/astock-live would fail at boot.
ASTOCK_V2_DB=/var/lib/astock-v2-rewrite/v2.sqlite3
# REQUIRED: the intraday ledger is a second database, not a table in the one
# above. Without this the kernel falls back to the relative path
# work/live/intraday.sqlite3, which only exists under a working directory it
# may not have; a fresh install would refuse to start.
ASTOCK_V2_LIVE_DB=/var/lib/astock-v2-rewrite/live/intraday.sqlite3
# Optional: directory of reviewed price sets (*.json published by
# scripts/publish_price_set.sh). Empty means valuation stays unavailable.
ASTOCK_PRICE_SETS_DIR=/var/lib/astock-v2-rewrite/price-sets
# Optional: bind the HTTP listener. Keep loopback and proxy through nginx.
ASTOCK_V2_ADDR=127.0.0.1:18765
# Persistent settings JSON for AI provider & long-running config. Keep it in
# the same writable directory as the live database: the default is
# <live-db-dir>/settings.json, and the service user cannot write elsewhere.
ASTOCK_SETTINGS_PATH=/var/lib/astock-v2-rewrite/settings.json
# Optional initial AI provider defaults (can also be configured in Web UI -> 设置):
ASTOCK_LLM_BASE=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
ASTOCK_LLM_MODEL=deepseek-chat
# ASTOCK_LLM_KEY=sk-your-key-here
